-- #1617 PERMUTATION PROBE — NOT RUN BY THIS GATE. It records the second half of
-- the observation, which neither graded file can carry: the wrong answer is
-- decided by the DECLARATION ORDER of the two impl blocks.
--
-- Byte-identical to main.mdk's program except (a) the two `impl` blocks are
-- swapped and (b) it prints the RAW tuple rather than the projection, because
-- the raw value is the whole point here.
--
-- Re-derive with one command (correct is (5, 9) — see main.mdk):
--   ./medaka run test/must_fail_fixtures/1617-fn-typed-impl-head-none-bucket/permutation.mdk
-- Measured 2026-08-14: prints (9, 9) at exit 0, where main.mdk's ordering prints
-- (5, 5). Both are wrong, differently — which is exactly why main.mdk pins a
-- projected Bool and not a literal tuple.
interface Sz a where
  sz : a -> Int
impl Sz (Bool -> Bool) where
  sz _ = 9
impl Sz (Int -> Int) where
  sz _ = 5
f : Int -> Int
f x = x + 1
g : Bool -> Bool
g b = b
main = println (sz f, sz g)
